{"id":"c3fd458de44fd001c280f643a0eaf79008953cb4","axis":"silent","repo":"vimeo/psalm","sha":"c3fd458de44fd001c280f643a0eaf79008953cb4","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/running_psalm/plugins/authoring_plugins.md","lines":["@@ -110,6 +110,7 @@ class SomePlugin implements \\Psalm\\Plugin\\EventHandler\\AfterStatementAnalysisInt"," - `PropertyExistenceProviderInterface` - can be used to override Psalm's builtin property existence checks for one or more classes."," - `PropertyTypeProviderInterface` - can be used to override Psalm's builtin property type lookup for one or more classes."," - `PropertyVisibilityProviderInterface` - can be used to override Psalm's builtin property visibility checks for one or more classes.","+- `AddCallTaintsInterface` and `RemoveCallTaintsInterface` - can be used to add or remove the taints of an argument going into a call, or of what a call returns, from the function-like called and the argument's offset and type (see [Wiring calls into the taint graph](#wiring-calls-into-the-taint-graph))."," - `DynamicFunctionStorageProviderInterface` - can be used to override signature for one or more functions. It means you can define variadic param list. Infer return type by input args. Define function templates. Also check out `Psalm\\Plugin\\DynamicFunctionStorage` to find out what api it brings for you to change function's definition."," "," Here are a couple of example plugins:","@@ -131,6 +132,77 @@ You can also specify an absolute path to your plugin:","     </plugins>"," ```"," ","+### Wiring calls into the taint graph","+","+`Codebase::addTaintedCall()` makes taint analysis follow a call PHP code doesn't make (a template calling a function,","+a configuration naming a method), wired as Psalm wires a PHP call of it. It returns the node of what the call returns","+(null without taint analysis). A plugin providing the return type of `call_through('function_name', ...$args)`:","+","+```php","+$node = $codebase->addTaintedCall(","+    'show',                     // 'ns\\function_name' or 'Class::method'","+    $argument_nodes,            // list<list<DataFlowNode>>: the nodes of each argument, by position","+    $argument_types,            // array<int, Union>: the types of the arguments, by position","+    $event->getCodeLocation(),","+    $source,                    // nothing is wired while its taints aren't tracked","+);","+","+return $node === null ? $type : $type->addParentNodes([$node->id => $node]);","+```","+","+```php","+function show(string $s): void {","+    echo $s; // TaintedHtml","+}","+","+/** @psalm-taint-sink ($kind is \"sql\" ? \"sql\" : null) $value */","+function query(string $kind, string $value): void {}","+","+/** @psalm-taint-escape ($escape is true ? \"html\" : null) */","+function maybe_escape(string $s, bool $escape): string {","+    return $s;","+}","+","+/** @psalm-taint-specialize */","+function specialized(string $s): string {","+    return $s;","+}","+","+call_through(\"show\", (string) $_GET[\"a\"]);","+call_through(\"query\", \"sql\", (string) $_GET[\"b\"]);                // TaintedSql","+call_through(\"query\", \"other\", (string) $_GET[\"c\"]);              // no issue","+echo call_through(\"maybe_escape\", (string) $_GET[\"d\"], false);    // TaintedHtml","+echo call_through(\"maybe_escape\", (string) $_GET[\"e\"], true);     // TaintedTextWithQuotes, no TaintedHtml","+call_through(\"specialized\", (string) $_GET[\"f\"]);","+echo call_through(\"specialized\", \"safe\");                         // no issue","+```","+","+Not wired: the overrides of a method (wire a call of each), by-reference parameters, callables given to callable","+parameters, and keyed stores (`@psalm-flow ($value) -> Store::$data[$key]`).","+","+`AddCallTaintsInterface` and `RemoveCallTaintsInterface` handlers add or remove the taints of an argument going into a","+call, or of what a call returns. Unlike `AddRemoveTaintsEvent`, their `AddRemoveCallTaintsEvent` has no expression: it","+gives the function-like called, the argument offset (null for what the call returns), its type and a location. Psalm","+dispatches it for PHP calls and for `addTaintedCall()` alike:","+","+```php","+public static function removeCallTaints(AddRemoveCallTaintsEvent $event): int","+{","+    return strtolower($event->getFunctionId()) === 'clean' && $event->getArgumentOffset() === 0","+        ? TaintKind::INPUT_HTML","+        : 0;","+}","+```","+","+```php","+function clean(string $s): string {","+    return $s;","+}","+","+echo clean((string) $_GET[\"g\"]);                     // TaintedTextWithQuotes, no TaintedHtml","+echo call_through(\"clean\", (string) $_GET[\"h\"]);     // TaintedTextWithQuotes, no TaintedHtml","+```","+"," ### Using Xdebug"," "," As Psalm disables _Xdebug_ at runtime, if you need to debug your code step-by-step when authoring a plugin, you can allow the extension by running Psalm as following:"],"additions":72,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/security_analysis/taint_flow.md","lines":["@@ -568,6 +568,10 @@ Plugins can add flows that annotations can't express with these `Codebase` metho","   can't carry those taints, as long as it holds the same value: `$validator->fails()` and `passes()` for a result of","   kind `validator`, `count($violations) > 0`, `$violations->count() === 0`, ... for one of kind `violations`. Call it","   from `afterExpressionAnalysis()`.","++ `addTaintedCall($function, $argument_nodes, $argument_types, $call_location, $source = null)`: wires a call of a","+  function or a method from the nodes and the types of its arguments, as Psalm wires a PHP call of it (sinks,","+  conditional sinks and escapes, flows, specialization), and returns the node of what it returns. See","+  [Wiring calls into the taint graph](../running_psalm/plugins/authoring_plugins.md#wiring-calls-into-the-taint-graph)."," + `tracksTaintFlow($source)`: false when taints aren't tracked there, e.g. when `TaintedInput` is suppressed. The","   methods above then add nothing."," "],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Psalm/Codebase.php","lines":["@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@"," use Psalm\\Internal\\Codebase\\TaintFlowGraph;"," use Psalm\\Internal\\Codebase\\TaintStore;"," use Psalm\\Internal\\Codebase\\TaintValidations;","+use Psalm\\Internal\\Codebase\\TaintedCall;"," use Psalm\\Internal\\DataFlow\\DataFlowNode;"," use Psalm\\Internal\\LanguageServer\\PHPMarkdownContent;"," use Psalm\\Internal\\LanguageServer\\Reference;","@@ -3113,6 +3114,112 @@ public function getTaintNode(","         return $node;","     }"," ","+    /**","+     * Wires a call of the function or method $function_id (`function_name`, `Class::method`) into the taint graph as","+     * Psalm wires a PHP call of it, for a plugin analyzing calls PHP code doesn't make (a template calling a PHP","+     * function, a configuration naming a method), and returns the node of what the call returns. To make an","+     * expression's value come from it, use `$type->addParentNodes([$node->id => $node])`.","+     *","+     * Each argument goes into the parameter taking it (the variadic parameter takes those after it): into its body,","+     * into the sinks of its `@psalm-taint-sink`, and into those of a conditional `@psalm-taint-sink (<conditional>)`","+     * that $argument_types resolve. The call returns what the body returns, what its `@psalm-flow` and its","+     * `@psalm-taint-source` give, without what it escapes, including what a conditional","+     * `@psalm-taint-escape (<conditional>)` that $argument_types resolve escapes. A call of a function-like whose calls","+     * Psalm specializes (`@psalm-taint-specialize`) takes and returns only its own. AddCallTaintsInterface and","+     * RemoveCallTaintsInterface handlers decide what each argument, and what the call returns, take and lose.","+     * A method call goes to the method only, not to the methods overriding it: wire a call of each to go to them too.","+     *","+     * Null without taint analysis, while the taints of $source are not tracked (see tracksTaintFlow()), or if","+     * $function_id has no storage. A function is looked up from the file of $call_location, then among all functions.","+     *","+     * @param list<list<DataFlowNode>> $argument_nodes the nodes each argument comes from, by position","+     * @param array<int, Union> $argument_types the types of the arguments, by position: a literal type decides the","+     *                                          conditions on the parameter taking it, an argument without a type none","+     */","+    public function addTaintedCall(","+        string $function_id,","+        array $argument_nodes,","+        array $argument_types,","+        CodeLocation $call_location,","+        ?StatementsSource $source = null,","+    ): ?DataFlowNode {","+        $graph = $source === null ? $this->taint_flow_graph : $this->getTaintFlowGraphOf($source);","+        if ($graph === null) {","+            return null;","+        }","+","+        if (MethodIdentifier::isValidMethodIdReference($function_id)) {","+            $method_id = MethodIdentifier::wrap($function_id);","+            if (!$this->classlike_storage_provider->has($method_id->fq_class_name)) {","+                return null;","+            }","+","+            $declaring_method_id = $this->methods->getDeclaringMethodId($method_id);","+            if ($declaring_method_id === null) {","+                return null;","+            }","+","+            $storage = $this->methods->getStorage($declaring_method_id);","+            // the nodes of the parameters the body of the method takes","+            $cased_function_id = FunctionLikeAnalyzer::getCasedBodyMethodId($this, $method_id);","+        } else {","+            $cased_function_id = ltrim($function_id, '\\\\');","+            $function_id_lc = strtolower($cased_function_id);","+            $storage = $function_id_lc === ''","+                ? null","+                : $this->getFunctionStorageOfTaintedCall($function_id_lc, $call_location);","+            if ($storage === null) {","+                return null;","+            }","+        }","+","+        return TaintedCall::wire(","+            $this,","+            $graph,","+            $cased_function_id,","+            $storage,","+            $argument_nodes,","+            $argument_types,","+            $call_location,","+        );","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * @param non-empty-lowercase-string $function_id","+     */","+    private function getFunctionStorageOfTaintedCall(","+        string $function_id,","+        CodeLocation $call_location,","+    ): ?FunctionLikeStorage {","+        try {","+            return $this->functions->getStorage(","+                null,","+                $function_id,","+                $call_location->file_path,","+                $call_location->file_path,","+            );","+        } catch (InvalidArgumentException | UnexpectedValueException) {","+            // not a function of the file of the call","+        }","+","+        foreach (FileStorageProvider::getAll() as $file_storage) {","+            if (isset($file_storage->functions[$function_id])) {","+                return $file_storage->functions[$function_id];","+            }","+        }","+","+        if (!InternalCallMapHandler::inCallMap($function_id)) {","+            return null;","+        }","+","+        // a builtin without a stub: its call map entry gives its sinks and flows","+        try {","+            return $this->functions->getStorageForSymbolLookup($function_id, $call_location->file_path);","+        } catch (InvalidArgumentException | UnexpectedValueException) {","+            return null;","+        }","+    }","+","     /**","      * The taint node of the property `Class::$name`: assignments flow into it, fetches read from it. The property","      * doesn't need to be declared."],"additions":107,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Psalm/Internal/Analyzer/Statements/Expression/Call/ArgumentAnalyzer.php","lines":["@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@"," use Psalm\\Issue\\PossiblyInvalidArgument;"," use Psalm\\IssueBuffer;"," use Psalm\\Node\\VirtualArg;","+use Psalm\\Plugin\\EventHandler\\Event\\AddRemoveCallTaintsEvent;"," use Psalm\\Plugin\\EventHandler\\Event\\AddRemoveTaintsEvent;"," use Psalm\\Storage\\FunctionLikeParameter;"," use Psalm\\Storage\\FunctionLikeStorage;","@@ -2059,6 +2060,29 @@ private static function coerceValueAfterGatekeeperArgument(","         }","     }"," ","+    /**","+     * What the call taint handlers add to and remove from an argument, where taint analysis runs","+     *","+     * @return array{int, int}","+     */","+    private static function getCallTaints(","+        StatementsAnalyzer $statements_analyzer,","+        string $cased_method_id,","+        int $argument_offset,","+        Union $input_type,","+        CodeLocation $arg_location,","+    ): array {","+        if (!$statements_analyzer->getTaintFlowGraphWithSuppressed()) {","+            return [0, 0];","+        }","+","+        $codebase = $statements_analyzer->getCodebase();","+","+        return $codebase->config->eventDispatcher->dispatchAddRemoveCallTaints(","+            new AddRemoveCallTaintsEvent($codebase, $cased_method_id, $argument_offset, $input_type, $arg_location),","+        );","+    }","+","     /**","      * @psalm-pure","      */","@@ -2139,6 +2163,16 @@ private static function processTaintedness(","         $added_taints = $codebase->config->eventDispatcher->dispatchAddTaints($event);","         $removed_taints |= $codebase->config->eventDispatcher->dispatchRemoveTaints($event);"," ","+        [$call_added_taints, $call_removed_taints] = self::getCallTaints(","+            $statements_analyzer,","+            $cased_method_id,","+            $argument_offset,","+            $input_type,","+            $arg_location,","+        );","+        $added_taints |= $call_added_taints;","+        $removed_taints |= $call_removed_taints;","+","         // printed by code only running from the command line: to a terminal","         if ($expr->getAttribute(CliOutput::PRINTED_ATTRIBUTE) === true) {","             $removed_taints |= CliOutput::HTML_TAINTS;"],"additions":34,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Psalm/Internal/Analyzer/Statements/Expression/Call/FunctionCallReturnTypeFetcher.php","lines":["@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@"," use Psalm\\Internal\\Type\\TypeExpander;"," use Psalm\\Internal\\Type\\TypeVariableTracker;"," use Psalm\\IssueBuffer;","+use Psalm\\Plugin\\EventHandler\\Event\\AddRemoveCallTaintsEvent;"," use Psalm\\Plugin\\EventHandler\\Event\\AddRemoveTaintsEvent;"," use Psalm\\Plugin\\EventHandler\\Event\\AfterFunctionCallAnalysisEvent;"," use Psalm\\Storage\\FunctionLikeParameter;","@@ -63,6 +64,7 @@"," use function array_values;"," use function count;"," use function explode;","+use function in_array;"," use function is_string;"," use function ltrim;"," use function preg_match;","@@ -1663,6 +1665,16 @@ private static function taintReturnType("," ","         $node_location = new CodeLocation($statements_analyzer->getSource(), $stmt);"," ","+        $call_added_taints = 0;","+        $call_removed_taints = 0;","+        if ($taint_flow_graph) {","+            $call_event = new AddRemoveCallTaintsEvent($codebase, $cased_function_id, null, null, $node_location);","+            [$call_added_taints, $call_removed_taints] = $codebase->config->eventDispatcher","+                ->dispatchAddRemoveCallTaints($call_event);","+            $added_taints |= $call_added_taints;","+            $removed_taints |= $call_removed_taints;","+        }","+","         $specialization_location = TaintFlowGraph::isCallSpecialized(","             $taint_flow_graph,","             $codebase,","@@ -1684,7 +1696,7 @@ private static function taintReturnType(","             $stmt->isFirstClassCallable() ? [] : $stmt->getArgs(),","         );"," ","-        if ($conditionally_removed_taints) {","+        if ($co